<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - HomeChoice lifts H1 shr, pays div.</title>
<headline>TABLE - HomeChoice lifts H1 shr, pays div.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, (cts)		7.5	   vs 5.4</p>
<p>    Interim div (cts)     2.0	   vs nil</p>
<p>    Net profit		7.5	   vs 4.4</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   11.6	  vs 6.8</p>
<p>    Tax			  4.1	  vs 2.4</p>
<p>    Interest paid	    0.4	  vs 1.9</p>
<p>    Turnover		  85.4	  vs 61.2</p>
<p>Div to be declared in August, payable September (no date)</p>
<p>On register - to be advised</p>
<p>Full name: HomeChoice Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said that it normally performed best in the second half of the year and, with current continued strong demand, expected growth to be maintained. As a result, it should be able to achieve its year forecast of 170 million rand turnover and 17.5 cts earnings per share.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +27 21 25-2238</p>
